WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.940
How well do you know the man who brought Napoleon
Dynamite’s Pedro to life?

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.020
It turns out that nowadays, he's living exactly
the way he wants to: as an actor, producer,

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.269
musician, and reality TV star.

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:14.960
Let's take a look at where Efren Ramirez’s
many skills have taken him.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.820
Ramirez wears many hats, but it seems that
his DJ one might be his favorite.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:24.080
He’s traveled the globe in this capacity,
performing at all kinds of private parties,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.500
festivals, and public gatherings.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:31.160
His prowess as a DJ and entertainer is also
aided by his wide and varied repertoire, which

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.760
includes everything from frothy disco favorites
to grinding electronica.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.640
Believe it or not, his music career actually
predates his film career.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.480
Nocturnal Rampage, a collective of musicians
he co-founded, began in 2000 and has a long

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.920
history of throwing raves and parties based
in Austin, Texas.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.190
His original mixes are available on YouTube,
and are well worth a look-in from fans and

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.390
Napoleon newbies alike.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:01:00.060
Ramirez isn't just a devotee of digital sound,
however - he's also an accomplished player

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.180
of more than a few traditional instruments.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.180
Though he's been known to play the violin
and use his voice for everything from rock

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.840
ballads to rap, he's perhaps best known as
a harmonica-player, and is often eager to

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.080
bust it out for an impromptu jam session.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:18.040
No matter where he may be, Ramirez always
seems ready to throw down the musical gauntlet.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:24.080
As he started so early, appearing in such
'90s gems as Kazaam and Tammy and the T-Rex,

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.280
it's no surprise that he's so comfortable
switching it up as a performer.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.860
His mother had a hand in that, putting him
in performing arts classes from a very young

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.740
age - a practice he later continued in order
to expand his social life.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.960
It's hard to remember nowadays how unlikely
a hit Napoleon Dynamite was.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.720
An oddly deadpan protagonist with a hairstyle
at least twenty years out of date?

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.960
Jokes centered around Jamiroquai, obscure
tiger-lion hybrids, and tater tots?

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.020
It's a movie that could only have come out
of the independent film scene - undeniably

00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:00.020
fresh without visible effort, perfectly bizarre
without ever feeling calculated, and, above

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.020
all else, indefinably addictive.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.980
It's no surprise, then, that Ramirez has continued
to keep at least one foot in the world of

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:07.560
indie movies.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:12.880
Since his turn as Pedro, he's starred in everything
from short films like Tomorrow's Yesterday

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.620
to searing biopics such as Endgame.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.780
But he's not too proud to show up in some
good old-fashioned popcorn blockbusters either,

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.069
with action thriller Crank and goofy comedy
Employee of the Month as notable additions

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:25.020
to his filmography.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.370
Ramirez seems to be an actor who keeps his
eyes on the stars — without ever forgetting

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.140
where he came from.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.940
Name an actor who's gained any ounce of fame,
and you'll name a collector of some kind.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:40.920
Guillermo del Toro has a house full of horror
paraphernalia; Nic Cage is so devoted to Superman

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.200
that he named his son after the Man of Steel
himself.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:48.840
Efren Ramirez, meanwhile, is devoted to cars
- so much so that it long predates his fame.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:54.000
In an interview with Motor Trend, Ramirez
set out his long-held interest and participation

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.520
in the California racing scene.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.459
He started with a "Frankenstein car," one
bequeathed to him by an older brother that

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.620
contained more pieces from other cars than
its original body.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.800
Though it wasn't much to look at, it was the
first of what eventually became a vast collection.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.740
He went on to note that his love of speed
doesn't just confine itself to cars - he also

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.659
loves to throw his mountain bike in the trunk
and take it to wherever he can cycle freely.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.660
“You ever take it off any sweet jumps?”

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.520
Actors in this day and age often find it advantageous
to diversify their audience.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:35.800
It's not enough to appeal to only the rarefied
indie connoisseur, the excitable fanboy, or

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.420
the swooning romcom fiend.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:42.560
Nor is it enough to stick to only one screen,
large or small — and with the growing prestige

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.700
of channels like HBO and Showtime, there's
no shame in television any longer.

00:03:47.249 --> 00:03:52.120
Yet even within the small sphere of television,
maybe sticking to one genre or format isn't

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:52.620
enough.

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:58.140
Ramirez, having conquered the worlds of indie
film, action beat-em-ups, HBO, animation and

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.740
more, has also dabbled in reality TV - and
appeared to have had great fun doing it.

00:04:03.529 --> 00:04:08.240
His most notable appearance was as a judge
on cycle eight of America's Next Top Model,

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.520
on which he fostered and assessed the contestants'
performances during an acting challenge.

00:04:12.749 --> 00:04:16.660
Appropriately enough, the episode was entitled
"The Girl Who Impresses Pedro."

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:21.821
Ramirez doesn’t seem particularly content
to sit on the sidelines of his career, nor

00:04:21.821 --> 00:04:24.380
to rest on his laurels in only one type of
job.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.990
In 2006's Employee of the Month, he played
a limp-spined "box boy."

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.550
“You’re the lowest of the low.”

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.360
“Yeah, the lowest of the low.”

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.860
“Aren’t you a box-boy too, Jorge?”

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:36.120
“Yeah, but he’s my box-boy.”

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.980
“Yeah, I’m his box-boy.”

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:43.520
He followed that up with a role in 2012's
Casa de mi Padre, a ludicrously over-the-top

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.260
parody of Latin soap operas.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.220
Then he was a janitor in 2016's Middle School:
The Worst Years of My Life.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:55.530
All of this, however, stands in stark contrast
to his boldest move yet: founding his own

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:56.600
production company.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:01.600
Powerhouse Pictures Entertainment is a joint
project with Chris Barrett, a director, producer

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.120
and author.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:07.450
A company which aims to produce across various
platforms and media, Powerhouse has long been

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:13.160
affiliated with After School, a documentary
exploring the story of Debra Lafave, the American

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:18.250
teacher who was arrested in 2005 for lewd
and lascivious battery of one of her 14-year-old

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:18.740
students.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.620
Clearly Ramirez is looking to spend more time
behind the camera as he moves on to the next

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.140
phase of his quirky career.

